VALUES (661, '1', $t$ASK 661: the Shared Library header comment is set to the library body, so the engine's Library Check lets a run start$t$,
  $t$The run-start check refused at 18:14 CST 2026-11-25 on engine 5d43650d (Wall 12265): the Shared Library header comment named "library sha 0f8a6b2950f7de68, 3859 lines" while the body was fb8658437cad8fbf, 3,910 lines. The engine's own Library Check node, after Debate Start, stops a webhook run with "pkgLIB2: Shared Library text sha ... differs" when the two differ, so the next run would have stopped at its first step. Change, one node (Shared Library), the header comment only: "library sha 0f8a6b2950f7de68, 3859 lines" becomes "library sha fb8658437cad8fbf, 3910 lines". Expected effect: the Library Check passes and the next run starts. Standing rule from the coordinator (18:24 CST): every engine write script checks the Shared Library header against the body before it writes and refuses on a mismatch. Not changed: any other node, the child, the database, a model setting, reasoning.$t$,
  'in part',
  $t$Written by W4 on the operator's press "Write it live" at 18:29 CST 2026-11-25 on W4's card (Wall 12270; audit 42475), engine 5d43650d to 66ba992d (426 nodes; the child aad0ad9c unchanged by W4's post), and read back MATCH by W1 (Wall 12271: 426 of 426 nodes equal to W1's rebuild, connections equal; against 5d43650d only the Shared Library differs; the header reads "library sha fb8658437cad8fbf, 3910 lines" and the body hashes to the same with 3,910 lines; headerParameters present on all 61 nodes; standing 31 PASS 0 FAIL; the child not checked by W1). After the readback W4's run-start check on 66ba992d gave GO (W4's message to the coordinator, 18:33 CST; not posted on the Wall). First build graded FAIL F1 by W1 (Wall 12266): its base was a saved fetch with headerParameters stripped, and written whole it would have removed the request headers of 61 nodes; rebuilt from a fresh live fetch (Wall 12268) and regraded PASS WITH N1 (Wall 12269; N1: W4's target file was not on the shared folder, so W1 compared the jsCode md5; the write rebuilds from a fetch in the same call). CAUSE AND MISTAKES: W1's stored fetches show the header stale on every live version from 393bca2e (ASK 641) through 5d43650d (ASK 654) (Wall 12267); no run started in that span, so the engine never threw. W4: its write scripts checked the pair Library Check and the standing set, not the header against the body (Wall 12265). W1: every build grade and readback in that span missed it, and at the ASK 654 grade it was listed as a harmless defect without reading Library Check (Wall 12266, 12267). W4 at the write: the script's final pair check used a relative path and failed to open its file after the PUT; rerun with full paths, PASSES, script fixed (Wall 12270). IN PART, because no run has been made since the write. NOT CHECKED by W3: the live engine; the write script's text; audit 42475 beyond its title and first 200 characters. RUN REVISION 43103 (this row; where a sentence above says that no run has been made, this paragraph is the later word): run ODV1-43103-gkg7el4e (debate_results 0731a1ea, row saved 11:20 CST 2026-11-27; the operator's launch 10:48 CST, ended 11:44 CST by W4's report, Wall 12767; engine 66ba992d and child aad0ad9c; google/gemini-4-hydrogen as the Oracle defending against meta/muse-spark-1.3; outcome UNGRADED, panel 0-0 with 3 not counted under the debate rule; three judgments stored (sonnet, sol, sol62); cost 7.5384; no debate_errors row after the launch). FIRST RUN, EXERCISED. The run passed the Library Check and reached Accept Models and the end: review_notes holds five AGREEMENT lines, the row is saved with all eight rounds and three judgments, and debate_errors holds no row after the launch (so no pkgLIB2 stop). W3 counts this as the first of the two live runs with no issue that the operator's rule of 10:38 CST 2026-11-24 asks; objective_met stays 'in part' and status stays 'read back' until the second.$t$,
